target/

# The library's lockfile is not committed — it is a library, and its consumers
# resolve their own.
/Cargo.lock

# The guest's lockfile IS committed, deliberately. `cargo risczero build` runs
# `cargo build --locked`, so the build needs it to exist; and the pin that makes
# the build work at all — enum-ordinalize held at 4.3.2, because 4.4.2 declares
# MSRV 1.89 against the guest toolchain's rustc 1.88 — exists nowhere else. Left
# out, a fresh clone resolves a newer version and fails, with nothing in the
# tree to explain why.
!programs/*/Cargo.lock
